---
// [DEMO-LISTING-1 2026-08-26] Pretty listing URL: /<username>/<slug>
//
// Owner decision 2026-08-26: listings get a shareable /creator/listing URL, and
// FOR NOW the page they render is the bazaar mockup from design/live-streaming/
// ("avaTOK Listing Details.dc.html") — look and feel only, hardcoded mock data,
// backend wiring comes later. The real data-driven page still exists at
// /l/<id> (ListingDetailView.astro); nothing here replaces it yet.
//
// ─── WHY THE HTML IS SERVED RAW INSTEAD OF PORTED TO ASTRO ───────────────────
// The mockup is a self-contained Design Component document: a <x-dc> template
// with {{ }} holes, a `class Component extends DCLogic` script, and the
// support.js runtime that binds them at load. Re-expressing 88KB of that as
// Astro/Tailwind is the actual port, and it is throwaway work until the design
// is signed off. So the document is shipped verbatim and Astro only owns the
// URL. When the design settles, THIS is the file to replace with a real
// component — the route can stay exactly as it is.
//
// ─── THE <base> TAG IS LOAD-BEARING, DO NOT REMOVE ───────────────────────────
// support.js resolves components as COMPONENT_DIR + "/" + name + ".dc.html"
// with COMPONENT_DIR = "." — i.e. relative to the DOCUMENT. Served at
// /dollykapoor/mock-listing, "./SiteHeader.dc.html" would resolve to
// /dollykapoor/SiteHeader.dc.html and 404, and every <dc-import> (header,
// footer, all six TruckBorder strips) would silently render nothing. The same
// applies to ./support.js itself and every assets/*.png. <base href="/demo/">
// re-points all of it at the copied folder in one line.
export const prerender = false;

// Vite inlines this at BUILD time, so there is no runtime filesystem read (there
// is no filesystem on Workers) and no self-fetch. web/public/demo/ is produced
// by scripts/copy-design-demo.mjs in prebuild — see that file for why it is a
// copy and not a second committed tree.
import mockupHtml from '../../../public/demo/avaTOK Listing Details.dc.html?raw';

const { username, slug } = Astro.params;

// Astro matches static routes before dynamic ones, so /about, /blog, /sign-in
// and friends still win over this catch-all. This guard is for the rest: a bare
// handle must not swallow asset-ish or malformed paths and answer 200.
const looksLikeHandle = /^[a-z0-9][a-z0-9._-]{1,30}$/i.test(username ?? '');
const looksLikeSlug = /^[a-z0-9][a-z0-9._-]{1,80}$/i.test(slug ?? '');
if (!looksLikeHandle || !looksLikeSlug) return new Response('Not found', { status: 404 });

const html = mockupHtml.replace(
  '<head>',
  `<head>
<base href="/demo/" />
<title>${slug} · @${username} · avaTOK</title>
<meta name="robots" content="noindex, nofollow" />`,
);

// noindex above and a short cache here, deliberately: this is a design comp on
// fake data. It must not be indexed as a real listing, and it must not be
// cached so long that the next design iteration is invisible for an hour.
return new Response(html, {
  headers: {
    'content-type': 'text/html; charset=utf-8',
    'cache-control': 'public, max-age=60',
  },
});
---
